# Shared Components

Catalog and status of every component: `Docs/shared-components.md`. Preview them in the gallery
(`Views/Dev/GalleryView.axaml`, currently the MainWindow content).

## Reuse first
Before writing UI, use what exists (`xmlns:ui="using:Mostawsef.Desktop.Components"`):
- Layout: `AppShell`, `NavMenu`/`NavMenuItem`, `TopBar`, `PageHeader`, `Card`, `Section`, `ListDetailsView`, `Divider`, `ResponsiveGrid`
- Forms: `FormField`, `FormSection`, `ValidationSummary`, `SearchBox`, `PasswordField`, `DateRangePicker`, `FileUpload`, `ImagePicker`
- Buttons: `IconButton`, `ButtonGroup` (+ styled built-in `Button`, `SplitButton`, `DropDownButton`)
- Data: `DataTable` (wraps `DataGrid`), `Pagination`, `Badge`, `Avatar`, `Scheduler`
- Feedback/overlays: `Spinner`, `LoadingOverlay`, `EmptyState`, `Modal`, `ConfirmDialog`, `DialogHost`
- Navigation: `Breadcrumb`, `Stepper`, `Wizard`
- Clinic (display-only): `PatientCard`, `PatientHeader`, `PrintPreview`
- Built-in controls (TextBox, ComboBox, AutoCompleteBox, CalendarDatePicker, TabControl, ...) are already themed: use them directly.

## Deferred components
DetailsView, StatCard, Chart, Timeline, Alert, Skeleton, ErrorState, Drawer, AppointmentCard, PrescriptionItem,
InvoiceSummary, VitalsDisplay are **not built**. Create one only when a screen needs it.

## Creating a component
1. Class in `Components/<Category>/<Name>.cs`, namespace `Mostawsef.Desktop.Components`.
   Expose `StyledProperty`s; use `DirectProperty` for read-only/computed values and internal commands.
2. `ControlTheme` keyed `{x:Type ui:Name}` in `Components/<Category>/<Category>Themes.axaml` (included from `Styles/Theme.axaml`).
   A subclass of a templated control needs its own ControlTheme or `StyleKeyOverride`.
3. Use only tokens, `{l:Tr ...}` for built-in text, `TemplateBinding` in templates. Mirror-safe (RTL) layout.
4. Visuals created in C# have no TemplatedParent: style them by class in `Components/ComponentStyles.axaml`.
5. Global styles beat ControlTheme styles: for state that must override a global button style, toggle a class (see `Button.secondary.active`).
6. Clinic components stay display-only (plain text/enum properties), no business logic or Contracts DTOs.
7. Add a demo to the gallery and update `Docs/shared-components.md`.
